Should we cross here?

256
00:09:11,298 --> 00:09:13,928
- My gosh. - It's a steep hill.

257
00:09:14,368 --> 00:09:16,238
- But when you're on a hill, - Yes.

258
00:09:16,398 --> 00:09:18,037
walking backward makes climbing the hill easier.

259
00:09:18,038 --> 00:09:19,268
- Try it. - It's easier that way.

260
00:09:20,068 --> 00:09:21,367
- You're right. - You're right.

261
00:09:21,368 --> 00:09:22,507
Yes.

262
00:09:22,508 --> 00:09:23,638
It's not that hard like this.

263
00:09:23,838 --> 00:09:24,978
You're right.

264
00:09:26,248 --> 00:09:27,648
(Out of breath)

265
00:09:28,148 --> 00:09:29,278
Hey, there's another one.

266
00:09:30,778 --> 00:09:32,077
(No matter how much they climb up...)

267
00:09:32,078 --> 00:09:33,087
- Hey, this is... - Wait.

268
00:09:33,088 --> 00:09:34,248
- This is a workout. - Is that the place?

269
00:09:34,918 --> 00:09:35,988
- Oh, this is... - We must go up there.

270
00:09:36,388 --> 00:09:37,918
Wasp, my gosh. This is...

271
00:09:38,858 --> 00:09:41,188
If you're late to school, running up these hills...

272
00:09:41,558 --> 00:09:42,558
Don't talk to me.

273
00:09:42,559 --> 00:09:43,898
- Jung Min. - The stairs...

274
00:09:44,598 --> 00:09:46,428
- Hold on. - Hey.

275
00:09:46,928 --> 00:09:48,027
- Hey, this is... - Wait.

276
00:09:48,028 --> 00:09:49,198
- It's a workout. - This is the place?

277
00:09:49,598 --> 00:09:51,297
- I bet back in the day, - What?

278
00:09:51,298 --> 00:09:52,498
gym teachers or the dean made students...

279
00:09:52,908 --> 00:09:54,608
- do the duck walk here. - Right.

280
00:09:55,468 --> 00:09:57,007
- If they're not properly dressed. - Right.

281
00:09:57,008 --> 00:09:58,008
Or if they're late.

282
00:09:58,278 --> 00:09:59,278
(Panting)

283
00:09:59,508 --> 00:10:02,248
(She's struggling more than anyone.)

284
00:10:02,378 --> 00:10:03,977
You're wearing the wrong outfit today.

285
00:10:03,978 --> 00:10:05,448
It's summer.

286
00:10:06,688 --> 00:10:08,348
- What do you call it? - My gosh.

287
00:10:09,148 --> 00:10:11,017
- Students. - You know what?

288
00:10:11,018 --> 00:10:13,088
- Since we came up high, the view... - What a great view.

289
00:10:13,658 --> 00:10:15,028
I can see all the way to Gangnam.

290
00:10:15,988 --> 00:10:17,657
My gosh. What an amazing view.

291
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:19,767
(The panoramic view of Seoul unfolds before them.)

292
00:10:19,768 --> 00:10:20,868
The view is amazing.

293
00:10:21,868 --> 00:10:23,037
That's the World Trade Center.

294
00:10:23,038 --> 00:10:24,937
Right. I can see all the way to Samseong-dong.

295
00:10:24,938 --> 00:10:27,068
- This is amazing. - Is that Namtaeryeong down there?

296
00:10:27,508 --> 00:10:28,908
- This place... - Isn't it?

297
00:10:29,108 --> 00:10:30,637
I can see Namtaeryeong in Seocho-gu.

298
00:10:30,638 --> 00:10:32,078
That's that thing in Samseong-dong.

299
00:10:32,678 --> 00:10:33,977
- That's the Star Tower. - Right.

300
00:10:33,978 --> 00:10:35,307
There's the World Trade Center.

301
00:10:35,308 --> 00:10:36,748
- I can see the Star Tower. - Yes.

302
00:10:37,078 --> 00:10:38,948
- Oh, your building? - It's not mine.

303
00:10:39,788 --> 00:10:41,287
- Why is that my building? - He's bragging about his building.

304
00:10:41,288 --> 00:10:43,317
Come on, Wasp.

305
00:10:43,318 --> 00:10:45,557
(Wasp is tackling Grasshopper.)

306
00:10:45,558 --> 00:10:47,387
You know what? This is...

307
00:10:47,388 --> 00:10:48,988
- We climbed up a lot. - the highest point we've been.

308
00:10:50,228 --> 00:10:52,157
- Hold on. There's no elevator. - Oh, my.

309
00:10:52,158 --> 00:10:53,227
And...

310
00:10:53,228 --> 00:10:54,997
(Fitness Room, 4th floor)

311
00:10:54,998 --> 00:10:56,898
- We must go to the fourth floor. - It's...

312
00:10:58,268 --> 00:10:59,397
(Another long hike to the 4th floor)

313
00:10:59,398 --> 00:11:01,008
- Is this the 3rd floor? - It's the 3rd floor.

314
00:11:01,568 --> 00:11:02,738
Hold on. This is...

315
00:11:04,008 --> 00:11:05,378
- Gosh, my water melted a lot. - Wait.

316
00:11:07,748 --> 00:11:08,748
It's here.

317
00:11:09,618 --> 00:11:10,817
Hey, I'm sweating a lot.

318
00:11:10,818 --> 00:11:12,648
Gosh, we already did our workout.

319
00:11:12,748 --> 00:11:15,188
- This is the place. - Let's go in. It's Jung Seo Woo.

320
00:11:15,718 --> 00:11:17,388
- Jung Seo Woo? - Seo Woo.

321
00:11:18,288 --> 00:11:19,488
- Oh, my. - There's a fitness room here.

322
00:11:21,188 --> 00:11:22,428
- In a school? - This is no joke.

323
00:11:22,488 --> 00:11:23,498
He's not here.

324
00:11:25,198 --> 00:11:26,367
This place is nice.

325
00:11:26,368 --> 00:11:28,497
(At the end of the hills and stairs...)

326
00:11:28,498 --> 00:11:31,067
(lies a workout paradise, the fitness room.)

327
00:11:31,068 --> 00:11:32,938
I didn't know there was a fitness room in a school.

328
00:11:34,168 --> 00:11:35,968
- Gosh, look. I'm sweating. - My gosh.

329
00:11:36,508 --> 00:11:38,677
By the way, where's our Whenever Guest?

330
00:11:38,678 --> 00:11:40,677
Our Whenever Guest must have asked us...

331
00:11:40,678 --> 00:11:42,507
- to come during the lunch break. - I guess so.

332
00:11:42,508 --> 00:11:44,448
It has to be a student then.

333
00:11:44,748 --> 00:11:47,788
No. Schoolteachers must also eat lunch.

334
00:11:48,318 --> 00:11:49,987
Of course, but... He must be here.

335
00:11:49,988 --> 00:11:51,058
I heard knocking.

336
00:11:52,088 --> 00:11:53,927
- Gosh, they're students. - They're students.

337
00:11:53,928 --> 00:11:55,188
(Smiling)

338
00:11:55,628 --> 00:11:57,458
My gosh. Look at these students.

339
00:11:57,958 --> 00:11:59,867
- Hello. - Are you Jung Seo Woo?

340
00:11:59,868 --> 00:12:01,428
- I see. - You're Seo Woo.

341
00:12:01,698 --> 00:12:03,067
Our Whenever Guests were students.

342
00:12:03,068 --> 00:12:06,308
Right? I got the feeling that they would be students.

343
00:12:06,438 --> 00:12:07,837
Should we move one down?

344
00:12:07,838 --> 00:12:09,038
Hello.

345
00:12:10,008 --> 00:12:11,737
I watched the movie trailer.

346
00:12:11,738 --> 00:12:13,407
- It's an honor. - The one for "Hope?"

347
00:12:13,408 --> 00:12:14,707
- Yes, "Hope." - "Hope."

348
00:12:14,708 --> 00:12:16,148
Na Hong Jin's "Hope."

349
00:12:17,878 --> 00:12:19,477
- I'm a fan of Na Hong Jin's works. - What?

350
00:12:19,478 --> 00:12:20,487
I'm a fan of his works.

351
00:12:20,488 --> 00:12:21,547
- Really? - Yes.

352
00:12:21,548 --> 00:12:23,158
- Jung Min... - Did you watch all of his movies?

353
00:12:23,218 --> 00:12:24,957
- I couldn't watch all of them. - I see. Right.

354
00:12:24,958 --> 00:12:26,927
- I'm not old enough for some. - Exactly.

355
00:12:26,928 --> 00:12:28,627
Right. He's strict about the age restrictions.

356
00:12:28,628 --> 00:12:30,258
When we were coming up...

357
00:12:30,958 --> 00:12:32,097
(The hill was incredibly steep.)

358
00:12:32,098 --> 00:12:33,568
There were so many stairs.

359
00:12:33,668 --> 00:12:35,897
So it feels like we're working out our legs when we come to school.

360
00:12:35,898 --> 00:12:37,037
Right?

361
00:12:37,038 --> 00:12:38,867
It's definitely a good workout.

362
00:12:38,868 --> 00:12:40,567
Our classmates hate the stairs. They loathe the stairs.

363
00:12:40,568 --> 00:12:41,607
Right?

364
00:12:41,608 --> 00:12:44,608
Some of them want to take the stairs to the founder and complain.

365
00:12:45,308 --> 00:12:46,577
(Their walk to school triggers complaints.)

366
00:12:46,578 --> 00:12:49,917
Hold on. We're in the Fitness Room.

367
00:12:49,918 --> 00:12:51,077
Do you do club activities here?

368
00:12:51,078 --> 00:12:52,577
- Tell us about this place. - What is this place?

369
00:12:52,578 --> 00:12:55,187
This fitness room used to be for our school athletic club.

370
00:12:55,188 --> 00:12:58,087
But we got permission from our gym teacher,

371
00:12:58,088 --> 00:12:59,117
so we get to work out here from time to time.

372
00:12:59,118 --> 00:13:00,827
That's why we're here.

373
00:13:00,828 --> 00:13:01,857
(They got permission to use it as they love working out.)

374
00:13:01,858 --> 00:13:04,597
Anyway, we read your letter earlier.

375
00:13:04,598 --> 00:13:06,327
You wrote that you worked with pens during the day...

376
00:13:06,328 --> 00:13:08,497
and workout equipment during the night.

377
00:13:08,498 --> 00:13:11,368
- Steel. - That must be why. Your build...

378
00:13:11,498 --> 00:13:13,537
I mean, you guys have a nice build.

379
00:13:13,538 --> 00:13:15,738
My gosh. You suddenly lifted your chest.

380
00:13:16,538 --> 00:13:17,538
Chan Hwi.

381
00:13:17,878 --> 00:13:19,707
Why did you lift your chest when I mentioned working out?

382
00:13:19,708 --> 00:13:21,678
No. The bench is slanted.

383
00:13:22,948 --> 00:13:24,777
I guess you work out a lot.

384
00:13:24,778 --> 00:13:26,647
I bet you can lift some serious weight.

385
00:13:26,648 --> 00:13:28,317
- Gosh, no. - No?

386
00:13:28,318 --> 00:13:30,288
I have a bad back.

387
00:13:30,858 --> 00:13:32,257
(I see.)

388
00:13:32,258 --> 00:13:33,457
Already?

389
00:13:33,458 --> 00:13:37,027
But why did you say that you worked out a lot in the letter?

390
00:13:37,028 --> 00:13:38,927
As for the introduction letter...

391
00:13:38,928 --> 00:13:41,668
So we've been in the same class since seventh grade.

392
00:13:41,868 --> 00:13:43,798
- The three of you? - Yes.

393
00:13:43,968 --> 00:13:46,237
Back then, we used to go...

394
00:13:46,238 --> 00:13:48,108
to Internet cafes, not the gym.

395
00:13:48,368 --> 00:13:51,207
We're happy when we enter the Internet cafes.

396
00:13:51,208 --> 00:13:53,248
But the reality sinks in by the time you walk.

397
00:13:53,608 --> 00:13:55,947
Then with Joon Ho's recommendation,

398
00:13:55,948 --> 00:13:58,048
we started to work out at the gym since eighth grade.

399
00:13:58,878 --> 00:14:01,387
- Are you in different classes now? - Yes, we are.

400
00:14:01,388 --> 00:14:04,117
- But we still get lunch together. - I see.

401
00:14:04,118 --> 00:14:06,688
(They're glued to each other even when working out.)

402
00:14:08,128 --> 00:14:11,597
(Post-workout)

403
00:14:11,598 --> 00:14:13,697
As we move up in grades, we have to attend more academies...

404
00:14:13,698 --> 00:14:15,527
- and our study load increases. - Right.

405
00:14:15,528 --> 00:14:17,367
We only get to see each other at the gym.

406
00:14:17,368 --> 00:14:20,107
Actually, we wrote to your show before graduating middle school.

407
00:14:20,108 --> 00:14:21,767
You wrote to our show in middle school.

408
00:14:21,768 --> 00:14:23,138
But we came to you when you started high school.

409
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:25,077
(Their luck came rather late.)

410
00:14:25,078 --> 00:14:26,477
We came to them in tenth grade.

411
00:14:26,478 --> 00:14:28,077
You must be quite flustered.

412
00:14:28,078 --> 00:14:29,107
- A bit. - Right?

413
00:14:29,108 --> 00:14:30,448
So a year ago,

414
00:14:30,578 --> 00:14:32,217
they watched our show and wrote the letter.

415
00:14:32,218 --> 00:14:33,617
- They were excited for it. - Right.

416
00:14:33,618 --> 00:14:34,947
They probably thought their story wasn't picked...

417
00:14:34,948 --> 00:14:36,817
and were going to focus on their studies.

418
00:14:36,818 --> 00:14:38,717
Then all of a sudden, our staff reached out to you.

419
00:14:38,718 --> 00:14:41,257
We came to you out of the blue when you didn't have any spare time.

420
00:14:41,258 --> 00:14:42,488
That's right.

421
00:14:43,128 --> 00:14:44,957
Exactly. We're sorry about that.

422
00:14:44,958 --> 00:14:46,098
- It's okay. - We didn't know.

423
00:14:46,798 --> 00:14:49,798
- How are your studies going? - Are you studying a lot?

424
00:14:50,068 --> 00:14:52,737
He gets the highest grades among us.

425
00:14:52,738 --> 00:14:54,167
- Seo Woo. - He's ranked third in our grade.

426
00:14:54,168 --> 00:14:56,007
(Ranked 3rd)

427
00:14:56,008 --> 00:14:58,908
- That's amazing. - Why are you bringing up grades?

428
00:14:59,378 --> 00:15:00,507
Let's listen to them.

429
00:15:00,508 --> 00:15:01,807
No, don't bring up grades.

430
00:15:01,808 --> 00:15:03,017
Let's talk about grades. He's ranked third.

431
00:15:03,018 --> 00:15:04,517
Kids are stressed out the most by their grades.

432
00:15:04,518 --> 00:15:06,748
How can we stop after hearing that he's ranked third?

433
00:15:07,748 --> 00:15:09,517
If he's ranked third,

434
00:15:09,518 --> 00:15:11,057
they must be ranked 4th and 5th.

435
00:15:11,058 --> 00:15:12,058
(Why would you ask them that?)

436
00:15:12,059 --> 00:15:15,087
Forget it. They're still growing. They're sweet kids.

437
00:15:15,088 --> 00:15:17,698
- It's cute they wrote to the show. - "They're still growing."

438
00:15:17,798 --> 00:15:18,998
- Seriously. - "They're sweet kids."

439
00:15:19,058 --> 00:15:22,227
Joon Ho, can I ask you about your grades?

440
00:15:22,228 --> 00:15:24,298
- I'm somewhere in the middle. - Okay.

441
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:26,298
What about you, Chan Hwi?

442
00:15:26,538 --> 00:15:28,867
- I'm somewhere around 100th place. - That's great.

443
00:15:28,868 --> 00:15:31,638
- What? - You need pretty good grades then.

444
00:15:31,778 --> 00:15:32,838
Then it's slightly higher.

445
00:15:34,878 --> 00:15:37,217
- You know what? That's great. - Right.

446
00:15:37,218 --> 00:15:39,347
- There's much room to improve then. - Yes.

447
00:15:39,348 --> 00:15:40,647
- You're only in tenth grade. - Right.

448
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,217
You can improve your grades if you set your mind to it.

449
00:15:42,218 --> 00:15:44,818
Besides, you might not want to do anything that requires good grades.

450
00:15:45,218 --> 00:15:46,358
But it does.

451
00:15:47,888 --> 00:15:49,128
All right then.

452
00:15:49,188 --> 00:15:50,427
If that's the case,

453
00:15:50,428 --> 00:15:51,898
- you have to study. - Okay.

454
00:15:51,998 --> 00:15:53,627
You should be studying a lot, Chan Hwi.

455
00:15:53,628 --> 00:15:55,298
- What's your dream career? - Good luck, Chan Hwi.

456
00:15:55,828 --> 00:15:58,867
I'm interested in psychology.

457
00:15:58,868 --> 00:16:00,038
Psychology?

458
00:16:00,508 --> 00:16:01,937
He's very thoughtful.

459
00:16:01,938 --> 00:16:03,037
- I bet. - He is.

460
00:16:03,038 --> 00:16:04,537
Do you read a lot of books, Chan Hwi?

461
00:16:04,538 --> 00:16:06,178
No, I barely read books.

462
00:16:07,078 --> 00:16:09,608
You keep asking about the exact opposites.

463
00:16:11,148 --> 00:16:12,747
- You... Listen. - Be quiet, Jung Min.

464
00:16:12,748 --> 00:16:14,988
Reverse whatever you want to ask.

465
00:16:15,448 --> 00:16:17,918
Okay. Come on.

466
00:16:18,288 --> 00:16:20,787
Is there a body part you want to show off?

467
00:16:20,788 --> 00:16:23,398
- My arms. - Show us your arms.

468
00:16:26,298 --> 00:16:29,198
(Impressed)

469
00:16:30,438 --> 00:16:32,437
Your biceps look amazing.

470
00:16:32,438 --> 00:16:34,008
Joon Ho seems happy about his arms.

471
00:16:34,168 --> 00:16:37,177
Anyway, we're here today.

472
00:16:37,178 --> 00:16:40,177
We should make good high school memories.

473
00:16:40,178 --> 00:16:42,407
Right. They're our first Whenever Guests...

474
00:16:42,408 --> 00:16:43,647
of our fifth season.

475
00:16:43,648 --> 00:16:46,217
- That's right. - I want to give them many presents.

476
00:16:46,218 --> 00:16:50,157
Ho Yeon and Jung Min are joining us today.

477
00:16:50,158 --> 00:16:52,457
I look forward to seeing their competitive side.

478
00:16:52,458 --> 00:16:55,758
So the fifth season comes with a new chance for you.

479
00:16:56,158 --> 00:16:58,527
(A new rule for the season)

480
00:16:58,528 --> 00:16:59,528
(Spare Chance)

481
00:16:59,529 --> 00:17:00,967
It's a new rule for the fifth season.

482
00:17:00,968 --> 00:17:02,327
- Whenever Guests... - Right.

483
00:17:02,328 --> 00:17:03,337
get one spare chance.

484
00:17:03,338 --> 00:17:05,968
But the options aren't all good.

485
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:08,508
Some of the options work against you.

486
00:17:09,068 --> 00:17:10,637
But it will be a random draw.

487
00:17:10,638 --> 00:17:11,838
(It depends on the Whenever Guests.)

488
00:17:11,908 --> 00:17:14,677
Probability-wise, there are more lucky chances than unlucky ones.

489
00:17:14,678 --> 00:17:17,417
If you want to use this spare chance when the time is right,

490
00:17:17,418 --> 00:17:18,947
- feel free to do so. - Yes.

491
00:17:18,948 --> 00:17:20,287
Here's the first one.

492
00:17:20,288 --> 00:17:22,688
When you crush it, you'll see what the present is.

493
00:17:24,618 --> 00:17:25,857
- Here you go, Chan Hwi. - It hasn't been long.

494
00:17:25,858 --> 00:17:26,858
(Grabbing)

495
00:17:26,859 --> 00:17:28,058
So he could eat it?

496
00:17:28,258 --> 00:17:29,357
- It's edible. - Is that edible?

497
00:17:29,358 --> 00:17:31,227
- It's edible. - It's edible.

498
00:17:31,228 --> 00:17:32,497
It's just food coloring.

499
00:17:32,498 --> 00:17:33,797
"Our muscles are ready."

500
00:17:33,798 --> 00:17:35,467
"This is a symbolic brand for gym rats."

501
00:17:35,468 --> 00:17:36,967
"Can we wear this brand now?"

502
00:17:36,968 --> 00:17:38,268
"Three outfits from Under Armour."

503
00:17:38,998 --> 00:17:42,008
This is a famous brand, right?

504
00:17:42,138 --> 00:17:44,377
The combined weight of the 3 major drills must reach 500kg to wear it.

505
00:17:44,378 --> 00:17:45,407
(The ultimate workout brand)

506
00:17:45,408 --> 00:17:47,648
The 3 of you can get 1 outfit each.

507
00:17:48,378 --> 00:17:50,718
Working out in that during summer will be great.

508
00:17:51,318 --> 00:17:53,147
(Ping-Pong on Dumbbells)

509
00:17:53,148 --> 00:17:54,717
(With 10 table tennis balls,)

510
00:17:54,718 --> 00:17:56,517
(they must hit the target balls on top of the dumbbells.)

511
00:17:56,518 --> 00:17:59,617
(Round 1: 2 target balls)

512
00:17:59,618 --> 00:18:01,488
But they're much farther.

