- Two tries. - We only have two tries left.

1039
00:36:36,564 --> 00:36:38,093
- It's... - You get nervous on the last try...

1040
00:36:38,094 --> 00:36:39,593
- and usually fail. - We must succeed.

1041
00:36:39,594 --> 00:36:40,594
- In one... - We must.

1042
00:36:40,595 --> 00:36:42,433
- In 1, 2, 3. Let's do this! - Let's do this!

1043
00:36:42,434 --> 00:36:43,663
The people ahead of me.

1044
00:36:43,664 --> 00:36:44,903
- Finish it, please. - Focus.

1045
00:36:44,904 --> 00:36:46,274
Let me move this.

1046
00:36:46,304 --> 00:36:48,204
Now the real game begins.

1047
00:36:50,104 --> 00:36:52,244
- Here I go. - The ninth try. Ready.

1048
00:36:52,874 --> 00:36:53,874
Set.

1049
00:36:57,214 --> 00:36:59,084
(Ninth try)

1050
00:37:00,054 --> 00:37:01,084
(1 shot, 2 kills)

1051
00:37:01,824 --> 00:37:02,824
Keep going.

1052
00:37:02,825 --> 00:37:03,854
(Off to a great start)

1053
00:37:03,884 --> 00:37:07,963
(Ninth try)

1054
00:37:07,964 --> 00:37:10,193
- I have to keep going. - The time is ticking.

1055
00:37:10,194 --> 00:37:11,493
- I'm sorry. - Okay.

1056
00:37:11,494 --> 00:37:12,494
- Okay. - Well done.

1057
00:37:12,794 --> 00:37:14,133
(Hit 3 balls)

1058
00:37:14,134 --> 00:37:15,204
- They'll make it. - Please.

1059
00:37:16,334 --> 00:37:17,974
Good. Nice one.

1060
00:37:18,334 --> 00:37:19,334
Okay.

1061
00:37:19,335 --> 00:37:20,674
- They'll make it. - Please.

1062
00:37:20,874 --> 00:37:23,343
(Ninth try)

1063
00:37:23,344 --> 00:37:24,444
Even just one.

1064
00:37:26,414 --> 00:37:28,084
One left.

1065
00:37:30,614 --> 00:37:31,883
(There's only one left.)

1066
00:37:31,884 --> 00:37:32,914
- We can make it. - One.

1067
00:37:33,754 --> 00:37:35,524
(The last target)

1068
00:37:35,984 --> 00:37:38,254
(Two players are left.)

1069
00:37:38,424 --> 00:37:39,454
One.

1070
00:37:40,154 --> 00:37:41,224
We can make it.

1071
00:37:42,024 --> 00:37:44,333
- One. - Five, four...

1072
00:37:44,334 --> 00:37:47,094
(Ninth try)

1073
00:37:47,294 --> 00:37:49,704
(Jae Seok's last ball)

1074
00:37:49,764 --> 00:37:51,504
Three, two...

1075
00:37:52,234 --> 00:37:54,233
(I'll make history with this one ball.)

1076
00:37:54,234 --> 00:37:55,344
- One. - A buzzer beater!

1077
00:37:56,474 --> 00:37:58,774
(A buzzer beater!)

1078
00:37:59,414 --> 00:38:01,344
- One. - A buzzer beater!

1079
00:38:03,314 --> 00:38:05,213
(Ninth try failed)

1080
00:38:05,214 --> 00:38:06,314
- One. - A buzzer beater!

1081
00:38:08,354 --> 00:38:10,483
Gosh, Jae Seok!

1082
00:38:10,484 --> 00:38:12,093
(That was so close.)

1083
00:38:12,094 --> 00:38:13,224
Seriously!

1084
00:38:16,705 --> 00:38:17,975
Still...

1085
00:38:18,094 --> 00:38:19,394
Really.

1086
00:38:19,594 --> 00:38:20,963
How did that one ball last?

1087
00:38:20,964 --> 00:38:22,633
I think we can use the 3-3-3-1 formation...

1088
00:38:22,634 --> 00:38:23,634
- again. - If only it had hit here.

1089
00:38:23,635 --> 00:38:26,173
Seriously, why couldn't we succeed?

1090
00:38:26,174 --> 00:38:28,744
That one ball you have feels like such a waste.

1091
00:38:30,504 --> 00:38:31,513
It's such a waste.

1092
00:38:31,514 --> 00:38:33,574
Come on.

1093
00:38:34,444 --> 00:38:35,713
I'll throw two balls.

1094
00:38:35,714 --> 00:38:37,014
This time...

1095
00:38:37,214 --> 00:38:39,754
We'll stick with 3-3-3-1, but I'll throw the last ball.

1096
00:38:40,584 --> 00:38:42,784
From what I can see,

1097
00:38:43,284 --> 00:38:45,823
we'll succeed within ten balls.

1098
00:38:45,824 --> 00:38:47,053
(Jae Seok is given 3 balls.)

1099
00:38:47,054 --> 00:38:48,363
- Let's give it a shot. - Okay.

1100
00:38:48,364 --> 00:38:50,524
It's our last try. Gather up.

1101
00:38:50,564 --> 00:38:52,833
- Really. - For goodness' sake.

1102
00:38:52,834 --> 00:38:54,234
(The last try of Round 3)

1103
00:38:54,634 --> 00:38:55,803
- In 1, 2, 3. - In 1, 2, 3.

1104
00:38:55,804 --> 00:38:56,863
- Let's go! - Let's go!

1105
00:38:56,864 --> 00:38:57,873
Split up the balls.

1106
00:38:57,874 --> 00:39:00,204
The last try.

1107
00:39:00,604 --> 00:39:02,043
It's fine even if they fail.

1108
00:39:02,044 --> 00:39:03,303
Yes, it's fine.

1109
00:39:03,304 --> 00:39:04,414
But we should succeed.

1110
00:39:04,774 --> 00:39:06,273
- Don't worry. - True.

1111
00:39:06,274 --> 00:39:07,274
Let's go.

1112
00:39:07,374 --> 00:39:08,443
The last try.

1113
00:39:08,444 --> 00:39:11,283
(Out of 10 total tries, they're on the last try.)

1114
00:39:11,284 --> 00:39:12,854
- Call it. - I will.

1115
00:39:13,854 --> 00:39:14,984
Here I go.

1116
00:39:15,184 --> 00:39:16,254
Ready.

1117
00:39:16,754 --> 00:39:17,794
Set...

1118
00:39:20,054 --> 00:39:25,233
(Last try)

1119
00:39:25,234 --> 00:39:26,264
Nice.

1120
00:39:27,094 --> 00:39:28,163
(1 shot)

1121
00:39:28,164 --> 00:39:30,204
(2 kills)

1122
00:39:30,834 --> 00:39:33,003
- Nice. - More to the left.

1123
00:39:33,004 --> 00:39:34,174
If only someone could...

1124
00:39:34,204 --> 00:39:35,544
(Last try)

1125
00:39:36,874 --> 00:39:38,673
- Hold on. - That one.

1126
00:39:38,674 --> 00:39:39,773
- It counts, right? - Yes.

1127
00:39:39,774 --> 00:39:41,313
- It counts. - Yes, it counts.

1128
00:39:41,314 --> 00:39:42,913
(There are only 2 target balls left.)

1129
00:39:42,914 --> 00:39:43,914
Okay.

1130
00:39:43,915 --> 00:39:45,613
(Jae Seok hit a whopping 4 balls.)

1131
00:39:45,614 --> 00:39:47,783
- Good. - That one counts, right?

1132
00:39:47,784 --> 00:39:49,853
- Yes, it counts. - Hold on. Get rid of it.

1133
00:39:49,854 --> 00:39:50,983
(Last try)

1134
00:39:50,984 --> 00:39:52,393
One last ball.

1135
00:39:52,394 --> 00:39:54,924
- One last ball. - Nice.

1136
00:39:57,494 --> 00:39:58,694
I think it'll work.

1137
00:39:58,734 --> 00:39:59,834
One ball.

1138
00:39:59,964 --> 00:40:01,733
(One ball!)

1139
00:40:01,734 --> 00:40:02,863
Please.

1140
00:40:02,864 --> 00:40:05,174
(Only one ball left)

1141
00:40:06,534 --> 00:40:09,173
(Last try)

1142
00:40:09,174 --> 00:40:10,344
Please.

1143
00:40:10,804 --> 00:40:11,974
Please, Yeon Seok.

1144
00:40:12,914 --> 00:40:14,013
(The last hope)

1145
00:40:14,014 --> 00:40:16,584
- Why must I finish the last one? - Jung Min.

1146
00:40:16,844 --> 00:40:18,154
- Watch the time. - Five seconds left.

1147
00:40:18,614 --> 00:40:21,983
- Jung Min, please. - Jung Min.

1148
00:40:21,984 --> 00:40:23,523
- Five seconds left. - Watch the time.

1149
00:40:23,524 --> 00:40:25,423
- You can do it. - Jung Min.

1150
00:40:25,424 --> 00:40:26,993
- Five seconds left. - Watch the time.

1151
00:40:26,994 --> 00:40:29,794
Four, three, two...

1152
00:40:33,734 --> 00:40:38,003
(The end)

1153
00:40:38,004 --> 00:40:39,104
It's a memory worth keeping.

1154
00:40:43,444 --> 00:40:44,514
It's a memory worth keeping.

1155
00:40:49,514 --> 00:40:50,583
It's a memory worth keeping.

1156
00:40:50,584 --> 00:40:52,554
That was so close.

1157
00:40:53,714 --> 00:40:54,754
That was so close.

1158
00:40:55,084 --> 00:40:56,624
- What a bummer. - It was a hard one.

1159
00:40:58,424 --> 00:40:59,854
Well done, everyone.

1160
00:41:00,794 --> 00:41:02,424
That was so close.

1161
00:41:03,594 --> 00:41:06,493
- That was so close. - No.

1162
00:41:06,494 --> 00:41:08,103
That was so close.

1163
00:41:08,104 --> 00:41:10,633
(The Prize Retrieval Team is on the move.)

1164
00:41:10,634 --> 00:41:11,873
(The sweatsuits, sneakers, and smartwatches are gone.)

1165
00:41:11,874 --> 00:41:13,204
Are you taking them?

1166
00:41:14,774 --> 00:41:16,204
Good job.

1167
00:41:16,904 --> 00:41:18,173
- No. - It's okay.

1168
00:41:18,174 --> 00:41:19,814
- Don't worry about it. - Jung Min.

1169
00:41:20,114 --> 00:41:22,144
How you took them is annoying.

1170
00:41:22,944 --> 00:41:24,044
On purpose.

1171
00:41:24,714 --> 00:41:26,154
What a real bummer.

1172
00:41:26,554 --> 00:41:28,154
When you practice...

1173
00:41:32,894 --> 00:41:35,164
- That was so close. - Really close.

1174
00:41:35,894 --> 00:41:36,924
It was...

1175
00:41:37,024 --> 00:41:38,363
You see,

1176
00:41:38,364 --> 00:41:40,933
we forgot that we're at a school.

1177
00:41:40,934 --> 00:41:42,403
I really wanted to win it.

1178
00:41:42,404 --> 00:41:43,703
Let's at least give these out.

1179
00:41:43,704 --> 00:41:45,674
- They looked so happy. - I'm sorry.

1180
00:41:45,874 --> 00:41:47,404
- Thank you. - I'm sorry.

1181
00:41:47,534 --> 00:41:48,644
Thank you.

1182
00:41:48,844 --> 00:41:50,003
Goodness.

1183
00:41:50,004 --> 00:41:51,174
It's a clock.

1184
00:41:51,974 --> 00:41:53,143
We'll hang it up in the classroom.

1185
00:41:53,144 --> 00:41:54,684
(A clock instead of smartwatches)

1186
00:41:55,784 --> 00:41:57,314
Things were going so well today.

1187
00:41:59,354 --> 00:42:01,624
No, it's still good.

1188
00:42:02,924 --> 00:42:03,983
They have to go to class now.

1189
00:42:03,984 --> 00:42:05,294
- It's a memorable day. - Really?

1190
00:42:05,324 --> 00:42:07,494
Good job, everyone. It was an honor.

1191
00:42:08,364 --> 00:42:09,823
- Study hard. - Thank you.

1192
00:42:09,824 --> 00:42:11,024
- Well done. - Gosh.

1193
00:42:11,334 --> 00:42:12,863
- I feel bad. - The strategy wasn't bad at all.

1194
00:42:12,864 --> 00:42:16,003
Yu Jae Seok, Yoo Yeon Seok,

1195
00:42:16,004 --> 00:42:18,004
Hwang Jung Min, and Jung Ho Yeon.

1196
00:42:18,874 --> 00:42:21,704
I'm a real fan of them. But it was kind of...

1197
00:42:22,704 --> 00:42:24,444
Well, it was...

1198
00:42:26,074 --> 00:42:27,774
Can I start again?

1199
00:42:28,344 --> 00:42:29,644
No, just go with it.

1200
00:42:29,844 --> 00:42:32,654
We'll keep working hard,

1201
00:42:33,484 --> 00:42:35,753
get perfect scores in the CSAT,

1202
00:42:35,754 --> 00:42:38,253
and meet Yu Jae Seok again...

1203
00:42:38,254 --> 00:42:39,724
in "You Quiz on the Block."

1204
00:42:40,294 --> 00:42:41,463
Whenever possible,

1205
00:42:41,464 --> 00:42:42,724
- post-workout. - Post-workout.

1206
00:42:44,664 --> 00:42:46,233
(The students have left for class.)

1207
00:42:46,234 --> 00:42:47,363
- This feels... - That was...

1208
00:42:47,364 --> 00:42:48,934
It left a weird aftertaste.

1209
00:42:51,204 --> 00:42:53,304
A feeling I can't put into words.

1210
00:42:53,574 --> 00:42:54,644
But really.

1211
00:42:54,904 --> 00:42:56,743
If you had hit the last ball,

1212
00:42:56,744 --> 00:42:58,914
- it would've been amazing. - For real.

1213
00:42:59,444 --> 00:43:00,874
The ball was so close.

1214
00:43:01,244 --> 00:43:02,744
What a shame.

1215
00:43:03,144 --> 00:43:05,084
- It was by a hair. - Exactly.

1216
00:43:05,854 --> 00:43:06,913
- We... - What time do we meet...

1217
00:43:06,914 --> 00:43:07,954
the next guest?

1218
00:43:08,584 --> 00:43:10,284
We meet them at 3:10pm.

1219
00:43:11,054 --> 00:43:12,623
We need to get lunch fast.

1220
00:43:12,624 --> 00:43:14,663
How about this?

1221
00:43:14,664 --> 00:43:17,293
Since we're at a school, why don't we get some street food?

1222
00:43:17,294 --> 00:43:18,533
- I'm in. - I don't mind anything.

1223
00:43:18,534 --> 00:43:19,933
Is that so? Ramyeon is...

1224
00:43:19,934 --> 00:43:21,933
- Don't you like ramyeon? - I love it.

1225
00:43:21,934 --> 00:43:23,303
How do ramyeon and gimbap sound?

1226
00:43:23,304 --> 00:43:25,474
- Street food, is it? - This gimbap place.

1227
00:43:25,634 --> 00:43:26,634
- Yes? - Yes.

1228
00:43:26,635 --> 00:43:28,273
- The one around the corner? - Yes.

1229
00:43:28,274 --> 00:43:29,303
- Let's go. - Okay.

1230
00:43:29,304 --> 00:43:30,543
Ho Yeon wants it.

1231
00:43:30,544 --> 00:43:31,544
(Street food as recommended by Ho Yeon)

1232
00:43:31,545 --> 00:43:33,444
It was a real bummer.

1233
00:43:34,514 --> 00:43:35,914
- Gosh. - The view here is...

1234
00:43:36,144 --> 00:43:37,613
It's nice even looking at it a second time.

1235
00:43:37,614 --> 00:43:38,683
(A breathtaking view amid the bittersweet moment)

1236
00:43:38,684 --> 00:43:42,323
If we saw this view after succeeding in the last round,

1237
00:43:42,324 --> 00:43:44,084
- we'd have been over the moon. - It would've been great.

1238
00:43:45,124 --> 00:43:47,224
I want to play a game again.

1239
00:43:48,094 --> 00:43:49,094
- We will soon. - We will soon.

1240
00:43:49,095 --> 00:43:50,964
I meant, play it now.

1241
00:43:51,564 --> 00:43:52,864
I may have become addicted.

1242
00:43:53,434 --> 00:43:55,563
- Our lunch bet. - Sorry?

1243
00:43:55,564 --> 00:43:57,333
- Our lunch bet. - Let's do that at the restaurant.

1244
00:43:57,334 --> 00:43:58,374
Okay.

1245
00:43:59,734 --> 00:44:03,704
I have two games in mind.

1246
00:44:04,674 --> 00:44:06,413
Please pick 1 of the 2.

1247
00:44:06,414 --> 00:44:08,213
- Two? - Did In Sung give you an idea?

1248
00:44:08,214 --> 00:44:10,613
The game In Sung suggested was...

1249
00:44:10,614 --> 00:44:12,983
to stop the stopwatch,

1250
00:44:12,984 --> 00:44:14,483
and the one...

1251
00:44:14,484 --> 00:44:18,323
- with the lowest time buys lunch. - Right.

1252
00:44:18,324 --> 00:44:19,953
- Yes. - This is the game I played...

1253
00:44:19,954 --> 00:44:21,253
with Director Hwang Dong Hyuk...

1254
00:44:21,254 --> 00:44:24,423
and the production team while filming "Squid Game."

1255
00:44:24,424 --> 00:44:25,463
You played several games...

1256
00:44:25,464 --> 00:44:26,464
- during work. - I did.

1257
00:44:26,465 --> 00:44:28,763
- What is it? - It's called the Crocodile Game.

1258
00:44:28,764 --> 00:44:30,763
- That one? - The game where you push a tooth,

1259
00:44:30,764 --> 00:44:32,533
- and the crocodile shuts its mouth. - Isn't there an app?

1260
00:44:32,534 --> 00:44:33,573
- Yes. - Right?

1261
00:44:33,574 --> 00:44:35,143
We played that game to see...

1262
00:44:35,144 --> 00:44:37,603
who would treat everyone to coffee.

1263
00:44:37,604 --> 00:44:38,744
There's an app.

1264
00:44:39,014 --> 00:44:40,143
Let's download it.

1265
00:44:40,144 --> 00:44:41,884
I already have it on my phone.

1266
00:44:42,684 --> 00:44:43,943
- Isn't this the place? - We're here.

1267
00:44:43,944 --> 00:44:45,614
Can we go in?

1268
00:44:45,714 --> 00:44:46,714
Isn't it closed?

1269
00:44:46,715 --> 00:44:48,154
- No. - It looks open.

1270
00:44:48,354 --> 00:44:50,383
- I was craving ramyeon. - Hi.

1271
00:44:50,384 --> 00:44:51,793
Street food in front of schools is great.

1272
00:44:51,794 --> 00:44:52,923
- Hi. - Are you open?

1273
00:44:52,924 --> 00:44:54,694
Rabokki also sounds nice.

1274
00:44:55,094 --> 00:44:57,264
- Did you bring a ball? - How about rabokki?

1275
00:44:57,464 --> 00:44:59,063
(Brought a ball in frustration)

1276
00:44:59,064 --> 00:45:00,693
What kind of gimbap do you like?

1277
00:45:00,694 --> 00:45:04,333
Aged kimchi and spicy chili.

1278
00:45:04,334 --> 00:45:05,604
Spicy chili sounds good.

1279
00:45:06,174 --> 00:45:08,374
I'm feeling rabokki.

1280
00:45:08,804 --> 00:45:10,103
- Order it. - One rabokki...

1281
00:45:10,104 --> 00:45:12,074
- Rabokki? - for sure. We can share it.

1282
00:45:12,874 --> 00:45:14,673
Ma'am, can we order kimchi noodles?

1283
00:45:14,674 --> 00:45:15,684
Yes, you can.

1284
00:45:15,714 --> 00:45:16,743
- Then... - One kimchi noodles.

1285
00:45:16,744 --> 00:45:17,944
I'd like Chapagetti.

1286
00:45:18,514 --> 00:45:20,613
Let's get pork cutlet to share.

1287
00:45:20,614 --> 00:45:21,783
- I'm in. - One pork cutlet.

1288
00:45:21,784 --> 00:45:23,524
- Nice. - One gimbap.

1289
00:45:24,054 --> 00:45:25,394
- Okay. - I want...

1290
00:45:25,594 --> 00:45:28,164
- Let's order individual dishes now. - I...

1291
00:45:28,464 --> 00:45:30,024
I'd like an egg ramyeon.

1292
00:45:30,564 --> 00:45:31,663
Egg ramyeon.

1293
00:45:31,664 --> 00:45:33,294
Should I have kimchi ramyeon?

1294
00:45:34,394 --> 00:45:37,034
All Ho Yeon has in mind is ramyeon.

1295
00:45:37,764 --> 00:45:39,233
- I... - Do you not have it regularly?

1296
00:45:39,234 --> 00:45:41,304
- Is it filling? - My nickname is Noodle Jung.

1297
00:45:41,844 --> 00:45:43,544
- I love noodles. - You do?

1298
00:45:44,074 --> 00:45:45,313
- Then... - Are you Whenever Possible?

1299
00:45:45,314 --> 00:45:46,673
Yes, ma'am. So you know the show.

1300
00:45:46,674 --> 00:45:47,873
Where were you just now?

1301
00:45:47,874 --> 00:45:49,913
- Daewon High School. - Daewon High School.

1302
00:45:49,914 --> 00:45:52,054
We failed Round Three.

1303
00:45:52,614 --> 00:45:54,954
- What did you want, Jung Min? - We're all upset.

1304
00:45:55,284 --> 00:45:57,254
I need to use the restroom. Where is it, ma'am?

1305
00:45:57,654 --> 00:46:00,493
To get to the restroom, turn when you see the building...

1306
00:46:00,494 --> 00:46:01,823
- Look, Ho Yeon. - and...

1307
00:46:01,824 --> 00:46:03,894
there's one downstairs.

1308
00:46:04,264 --> 00:46:06,333
(Floating in midair)

1309
00:46:06,334 --> 00:46:08,204
Did you bring one with you?

1310
00:46:09,034 --> 00:46:10,163
It was my go-to as a kid.

1311
00:46:10,164 --> 00:46:11,164
(Copying right away)

1312
00:46:11,165 --> 00:46:12,174
That's it.

1313
00:46:13,474 --> 00:46:14,474
(Laughing)

1314
00:46:14,475 --> 00:46:15,773
Let's stop for now.

1315
00:46:15,774 --> 00:46:17,844
Looks like you two are still pretty disappointed.

1316
00:46:18,074 --> 00:46:19,944
It's just that...

1317
00:46:20,244 --> 00:46:22,913
What we wanted was to hit the ball...

1318
00:46:22,914 --> 00:46:24,484
at the buzzer...

1319
00:46:24,584 --> 00:46:27,913
and taste victory.

1320
00:46:27,914 --> 00:46:29,224
- Yes. - It was a hard one.

1321
00:46:29,424 --> 00:46:33,654
Now that Director Na Hong Jin's "Hope" has been released,

1322
00:46:34,294 --> 00:46:36,964
